WEBVTT

00:03:29.297 --> 00:03:30.563
in a sequence.

00:03:30.563 --> 00:03:32.997
If it came across a roadblock
on the first path,

00:03:32.997 --> 00:03:35.263
it would simply rule
that out as a solution,

00:03:35.297 --> 00:03:37.030
revert to its original position

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:38.930
and try the next logical path,

00:03:38.963 --> 00:03:42.530
and so on and so forth
until it found the right solution.

00:03:42.563 --> 00:03:46.897
A quantum computer could
test every single pathway

00:03:46.897 --> 00:03:48.663
at the same time,

00:03:48.663 --> 00:03:54.897
in effect, solving the maze
in only a single try.

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:56.097
As it happens,

00:03:56.097 --> 00:04:00.697
many complex problems are characterized
by this mazelike quality,